IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition: s 76B -- the company's power to acquire its own shares.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Lines 8312-8507 of inputs/CoA1967.txt (a rendering, not the official text).
--
-- WHAT IS HERE. The power to purchase or acquire (1), the shares it covers (2), the 20% limits on ordinary shares and stocks and on
-- non-redeemable preference shares with their bases (3) to (3E), the relevant period (4), cancellation and its effect (5) to (6),
-- what a private company lodges (7) and when the purchase takes effect (8), what a public company's directors lodge and by when (9),
-- and the saving for Court orders (10).
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER. A function answers MAYBE BOOLEAN: JUST TRUE is yes, JUST FALSE is the text saying no in its own words,
-- NOTHING is "the text does not say". A caller never turns NOTHING into FALSE. Every JUST FALSE and every NOTHING carries a comment
-- that says which kind it is; the tags {F-..} point at the fork register and {MR-a}, {MR-b} at the marginal readings for a lawyer in NOTES.md.
-- Facts the text hands to the constitution, the Minister, the prescribed form or the Registrar are inputs, named for the fact.
-- Dates are Date day month year. A period is counted only by sg-periods.l4; a day count "beginning with" or "ending with" a day uses the
-- keel's function with the count less one (fork F-P1, and NEEDS-CORE.md).

§ `Section 76B(1) and (2): the power, and the shares it covers`

-- src:8314 | 76B.—(1) Despite section 76, a company may, in accordance with
-- src:8315 | this section and sections 76C to 76G, purchase or otherwise acquire
-- src:8316 | shares issued by it if it is expressly permitted to do so by its
-- src:8317 | constitution.
@ref s 76B(1) (src:8314-8317)
GIVEN `the company's constitution expressly permits it to purchase or acquire its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with section 76B and sections 76C to 76G` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(1) the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it` MEANS
    IF    `the company's constitution expressly permits it to purchase or acquire its own shares`
      AND `the purchase or acquisition is made in accordance with section 76B and sections 76C to 76G`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a grant ("a company may, in accordance with this section and sections 76C to 76G, purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it if it is expressly permitted to do so by its constitution") whose "if" gate failed; the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1 {F-B1} {MR-b}

-- src:8321 | (2) This section and sections 76C to 76G apply to ordinary shares,
-- src:8322 | stocks and preference shares.
@ref s 76B(2) (src:8321-8322)
GIVEN `the shares are ordinary shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are stocks` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the shares are preference shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(2) section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares` MEANS
    IF    `the shares are ordinary shares` OR `the shares are stocks` OR `the shares are preference shares`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "apply to ordinary shares, stocks and preference shares" names three kinds of share with no "only"; a scope limit, so a share of no named kind is outside it (the periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c)) {F-B2} {MR-b}

§ `Section 76B(3) to (3E): the 20% limits`

-- (3E) For the purposes of this section, any of the company's ordinary shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded.
-- src:8384 | (3E) For the purposes of this section, any of the company’s ordinary
-- src:8385 | shares held as treasury shares is to be disregarded.
@ref s 76B(3E) (src:8384-8385)
GIVEN `the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class, treasury shares included` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those ordinary shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76B(3E) the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class that counts` MEANS
    `the number of the company's ordinary shares in the class, treasury shares included` MINUS `the number of those ordinary shares held as treasury shares`

-- (3), (3B): "20% (or such other percentage as the Minister may by notification prescribe)": 20 is the Act's own figure; the Minister's is an input.
-- src:8324 | (3) The total number of ordinary shares and stocks in any class that
-- src:8325 | may be purchased or acquired by a company during the relevant
-- src:8326 | period must not exceed 20% (or such other percentage as the Minister
-- src:8327 | may by notification prescribe) of the total number of ordinary shares
-- src:8328 | and stocks of the company in that class ascertained as at the date of
-- src:8329 | any resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E
-- src:8330 | unless —
@ref s 76B(3) (src:8324-8330)
GIVEN `the Minister has prescribed another percentage by notification` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the percentage the Minister has prescribed by notification` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76B(3) the percentage that applies` MEANS
    IF `the Minister has prescribed another percentage by notification`
    THEN `the percentage the Minister has prescribed by notification`
    ELSE 20

-- (3A): where the company has reduced its share capital under s 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under s 78I, the total number of
-- ordinary shares and stocks in the class is, "despite subsection (3)(a) and (b)", the total as altered. Reading A (fork F-B3): the limit still
-- bites and is measured against the altered total; (3)(a) and (b) do not lift it.
-- src:8342 | (3A) Where a company has reduced its share capital by a special
-- src:8343 | resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order
-- src:8344 | under section 78I, the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of
-- src:8345 | the company in any class is, despite subsection (3)(a) and (b), taken to
-- src:8346 | be the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in
-- src:8351 | that class as altered by the special resolution of the company or the
-- src:8352 | order of the Court, as the case may be.
@ref s 76B(3A) (src:8342-8352)
GIVEN `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as at the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76B(3A) the total number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the limit is measured against` MEANS
    IF `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I`
    THEN `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order`
    ELSE `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in the class as at the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`

-- (3): the limit is a bar. TRUE: the number bought in the relevant period is more than the percentage of the base, so the company may not buy it.
-- src:8324 | (3) The total number of ordinary shares and stocks in any class that
-- src:8325 | may be purchased or acquired by a company during the relevant
-- src:8326 | period must not exceed 20% (or such other percentage as the Minister
-- src:8327 | may by notification prescribe) of the total number of ordinary shares
-- src:8328 | and stocks of the company in that class ascertained as at the date of
-- src:8329 | any resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E
-- src:8330 | unless —
-- src:8332 | (a) the company has, at any time during the relevant period,
-- src:8333 | reduced its share capital by a special resolution under
-- src:8334 | section 78B or 78C; or
-- src:8336 | (b) the Court has, at any time during the relevant period, made
-- src:8337 | an order under section 78I approving the reduction of share
-- src:8338 | capital of the company.
@ref s 76B(3) (src:8324-8338)
GIVEN `the number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the limit is measured against` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage that applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(3) the number purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceeds the limit` MEANS
    IF (`the number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` TIMES 100)
         GREATER THAN (`the percentage that applies` TIMES `the total number of ordinary shares and stocks in the class that the limit is measured against`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not exceed 20% (or such other percentage as the Minister may by notification prescribe) of the total number of ordinary shares and stocks of the company in that class" -- a number that does not exceed the limit is not barred by this subsection {F-B3} {MR-a}

-- (3C): the same for non-redeemable preference shares, measured against the altered total after a reduction or order.
-- src:8372 | (3C) Where a company has reduced its share capital by a special
-- src:8373 | resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order
-- src:8374 | under section 78I, the total number of non‑redeemable preference
-- src:8375 | shares of the company in any class is, despite subsection (3B)(a) and
-- src:8376 | (b), taken to be the total number of non‑redeemable preference shares
-- src:8377 | of the company in that class as altered by the special resolution of the
-- src:8378 | company or the order of the Court, as the case may be.
@ref s 76B(3C) (src:8372-8378)
GIVEN `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares of the company in the class as at the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 76B(3C) the total number of non-redeemable preference shares in the class that the limit is measured against` MEANS
    IF `the company has reduced its share capital by a special resolution under section 78B or 78C, or the Court has made an order under section 78I`
    THEN `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares of the company in the class as altered by the special resolution or the order`
    ELSE `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares of the company in the class as at the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`

-- src:8354 | (3B) The total number of preference shares in any class which are
-- src:8355 | not redeemable under section 70 that may be purchased or acquired
-- src:8356 | by a company during the relevant period must not exceed 20% (or
-- src:8357 | such other percentage as the Minister may by notification prescribe)
-- src:8358 | of the total number of non‑redeemable preference shares of the
-- src:8359 | company in that class ascertained as at the date of any resolution
-- src:8360 | passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E, unless —
-- src:8362 | (a) the company has, at any time during the relevant period,
-- src:8363 | reduced its share capital by a special resolution under
-- src:8364 | section 78B or 78C; or
-- src:8366 | (b) the Court has, at any time during the relevant period, made
-- src:8367 | an order under section 78I approving the reduction of share
-- src:8368 | capital of the company.
@ref s 76B(3B) (src:8354-8368)
GIVEN `the number of non-redeemable preference shares in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares in the class that the limit is measured against` IS A NUMBER
      `the percentage that applies` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(3B) the number of non-redeemable preference shares purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceeds the limit` MEANS
    IF (`the number of non-redeemable preference shares in the class that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` TIMES 100)
         GREATER THAN (`the percentage that applies` TIMES `the total number of non-redeemable preference shares in the class that the limit is measured against`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must not exceed 20% (or such other percentage as the Minister may by notification prescribe) of the total number of non-redeemable preference shares of the company in that class" {F-B3} {MR-a}

-- src:8380 | (3D) There is no limit on the number of redeemable preference
-- src:8381 | shares that may be purchased or acquired by a company during the
-- src:8382 | relevant period.
@ref s 76B(3D) (src:8380-8382)
GIVEN `the number of redeemable preference shares that the company has purchased or acquired in the relevant period` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(3D) the number of redeemable preference shares purchased or acquired in the relevant period exceeds a limit` MEANS
    JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "There is no limit on the number of redeemable preference shares that may be purchased or acquired by a company during the relevant period" (a flat negative; the number is accepted so that a caller can state it, and no number changes the answer) {MR-a}

§ `Section 76B(4): the relevant period`

-- (4)(b): the period expires on the date of the next annual general meeting "is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier".
-- src:8397 | (b) expiring on the date the next annual general meeting is or is
-- src:8398 | required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier.
@ref s 76B(4)(b) (src:8397-8398)
GIVEN `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76B(4)(b) the date the relevant period expires` MEANS
    IF `the date the next annual general meeting is held` AT MOST `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
    THEN `the date the next annual general meeting is held`
    ELSE `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`

-- src:8387 | (4) In subsections (3), (3B) and (3D), “relevant period” means the
-- src:8388 | period —
-- src:8390 | (a) commencing from the date of a resolution passed pursuant
-- src:8391 | to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E (as the case may be);
-- src:8392 | and
-- src:8397 | (b) expiring on the date the next annual general meeting is or is
-- src:8398 | required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier.
@ref s 76B(4) (src:8387-8398)
GIVEN `the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is held` IS A DATE
      `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held` IS A DATE
      `the date asked` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(4) the date is within the relevant period` MEANS
    IF    `the date asked` AT LEAST `the date of the resolution passed pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`
      AND `the date asked` AT MOST `s 76B(4)(b) the date the relevant period expires` `the date the next annual general meeting is held` `the date the next annual general meeting is required by law to be held`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“relevant period” means the period — (a) commencing from the date of a resolution ...; and (b) expiring on the date the next annual general meeting is or is required by law to be held, whichever is the earlier" (a "means" definition; both end days counted, fork F-B4) {F-B4}

§ `Section 76B(5) and (6): cancellation on purchase or acquisition`

-- src:8402 | (5) Ordinary shares that are purchased or acquired by a company
-- src:8403 | pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E are, unless held in
-- src:8404 | treasury in accordance with section 76H, deemed to be cancelled
-- src:8405 | immediately on purchase or acquisition.
@ref s 76B(5) (src:8402-8405)
GIVEN `the ordinary shares are purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the ordinary shares are held in treasury in accordance with section 76H` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(5) the ordinary shares are deemed to be cancelled immediately on purchase or acquisition` MEANS
    IF NOT `the ordinary shares are purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming covers "ordinary shares that are purchased or acquired by a company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E"; shares acquired some other way are outside it {F-B5} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the ordinary shares are held in treasury in accordance with section 76H`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless held in treasury in accordance with section 76H" {F-B5} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

-- src:8407 | (5A) Preference shares that are purchased or acquired by a
-- src:8408 | company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E are deemed
-- src:8409 | to be cancelled immediately on purchase or acquisition.
@ref s 76B(5A) (src:8407-8409)
GIVEN `the preference shares are purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(5A) the preference shares are deemed to be cancelled immediately on purchase or acquisition` MEANS
    IF `the preference shares are purchased or acquired by the company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the deeming covers "preference shares that are purchased or acquired by a company pursuant to section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E"; shares acquired some other way are outside it {MR-b}

-- src:8411 | (6) On the cancellation of a share under subsection (5) or (5A), the
-- src:8412 | rights and privileges attached to that share expire.
@ref s 76B(6) (src:8411-8412)
GIVEN `the share has been cancelled under section 76B(5) or (5A)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(6) the rights and privileges attached to the share expire` MEANS
    IF `the share has been cancelled under section 76B(5) or (5A)`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "On the cancellation of a share under subsection (5) or (5A), the rights and privileges attached to that share expire"; a share not so cancelled is outside the subsection {MR-b}

§ `Section 76B(7) and (8): the private company`

DECLARE `s 76B(7)(b) notice of purchase or acquisition` HAS
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice is in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the date of the purchase or acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares purchased or acquired` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares held as treasury shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the company's issued share capital before the purchase or acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the company's issued share capital after the purchase or acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the amount of consideration paid by the company for the purchase or acquisition of the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states whether the shares were purchased or acquired out of the profits or the capital of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
    `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states such other particulars as may be required in the prescribed form` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:8421 | (b) a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form
-- src:8422 | with the following particulars:
-- src:8424 | (i) the date of the purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8426 | (ii) the number of shares purchased or acquired;
-- src:8428 | (iii) the number of shares cancelled;
-- src:8430 | (iv) the number of shares held as treasury shares;
-- src:8432 | (v) the company’s issued share capital before the
-- src:8433 | purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8435 | (vi) the company’s issued share capital after the purchase
-- src:8436 | or acquisition;
-- src:8438 | (vii) the amount of consideration paid by the company for
-- src:8439 | the purchase or acquisition of the shares;
-- src:8441 | (viii) whether the shares were purchased or acquired out of
-- src:8442 | the profits or the capital of the company;
-- src:8447 | (ix) such other particulars as may be required in the
-- src:8448 | prescribed form.
@ref s 76B(7)(b) (src:8421-8448)
GIVEN notice IS A `s 76B(7)(b) notice of purchase or acquisition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(7)(b) the notice of purchase or acquisition is in the prescribed form and has the particulars` MEANS
    IF    notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice is in the prescribed form`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the date of the purchase or acquisition`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares purchased or acquired`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares cancelled`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the number of shares held as treasury shares`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the company's issued share capital before the purchase or acquisition`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the company's issued share capital after the purchase or acquisition`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states the amount of consideration paid by the company for the purchase or acquisition of the shares`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states whether the shares were purchased or acquired out of the profits or the capital of the company`
      AND notice's `s 76B(7)(b) the notice states such other particulars as may be required in the prescribed form`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form with the following particulars: (i) ... (ix) such other particulars as may be required in the prescribed form" (a description the notice must fit; the provision's own question) {F-B6} {MR-a}

-- src:8414 | (7) A private company may purchase or acquire any of its shares
-- src:8415 | under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E by lodging the following with
-- src:8416 | the Registrar:
-- src:8418 | (a) a copy of a resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D,
-- src:8419 | 76DA or 76E;
-- src:8421 | (b) a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form
-- src:8422 | with the following particulars:
-- src:8424 | (i) the date of the purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8426 | (ii) the number of shares purchased or acquired;
-- src:8428 | (iii) the number of shares cancelled;
-- src:8430 | (iv) the number of shares held as treasury shares;
-- src:8432 | (v) the company’s issued share capital before the
-- src:8433 | purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8435 | (vi) the company’s issued share capital after the purchase
-- src:8436 | or acquisition;
-- src:8438 | (vii) the amount of consideration paid by the company for
-- src:8439 | the purchase or acquisition of the shares;
-- src:8441 | (viii) whether the shares were purchased or acquired out of
-- src:8442 | the profits or the capital of the company;
-- src:8447 | (ix) such other particulars as may be required in the
-- src:8448 | prescribed form.
@ref s 76B(7) (src:8414-8448)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of a resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E` IS A BOOLEAN
      notice IS A `s 76B(7)(b) notice of purchase or acquisition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(7) the private company has purchased or acquired its shares by lodging what the subsection lists` MEANS
    IF    `the company is a private company`
      AND `the company has lodged with the Registrar a copy of a resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E`
      AND `s 76B(7)(b) the notice of purchase or acquisition is in the prescribed form and has the particulars` notice EQUALS JUST TRUE
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "A private company may purchase or acquire any of its shares under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E by lodging the following with the Registrar"; a grant of a way of doing it, with no word excluding any other way; a company that is not private, or that has not lodged both, is outside the grant (the grant rule of 2026-11-12, limit 1) {F-B7} {MR-b}

-- (8): "does not take effect until" -- the bar form of the ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d): TRUE before the register is updated, FALSE after.
-- src:8452 | (8) A purchase or acquisition by a private company on or after
-- src:8453 | 3 January 2016 does not take effect until the electronic register of
-- src:8454 | members of the company is updated by the Registrar under
-- src:8455 | section 196A(5).
@ref s 76B(8) (src:8452-8455)
GIVEN `the company is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date of the purchase or acquisition` IS A DATE
      `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(8) the purchase or acquisition cannot yet take effect` MEANS
    IF    (NOT `the company is a private company`)
       OR `the date of the purchase or acquisition` LESS THAN `the day 3 January 2016`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the subsection speaks of "a purchase or acquisition by a private company on or after 3 January 2016"; any other purchase is outside it {F-B8} {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF `the electronic register of members of the company has been updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)`
          THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not take effect until the electronic register of members of the company is updated by the Registrar under section 196A(5)" -- once it is updated the bar is gone (ruling of 2026-11-05, item (d)) {F-B8} {MR-a}
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 76B(9): the public company`

-- (9)(c): for the purposes of this section, shares are deemed to be purchased or acquired on the date on which the company would, apart from
-- subsection (5), become entitled to exercise the rights attached to the shares. The 30 days of (9)(b) run from that day.
-- src:8459 | (9) Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by
-- src:8460 | it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E —
-- src:8498 | (c) for the purposes of this section, shares are deemed to be
-- src:8499 | purchased or acquired on the date on which the company
-- src:8500 | would, apart from subsection (5), become entitled to
-- src:8501 | exercise the rights attached to the shares.
@ref s 76B(9)(c) (src:8459-8501)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date on which the company would, apart from section 76B(5), become entitled to exercise the rights attached to the shares` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 76B(9)(c) the date on which the shares are deemed to be purchased or acquired` MEANS
    IF `the company is a public company`
    THEN JUST `the date on which the company would, apart from section 76B(5), become entitled to exercise the rights attached to the shares`
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): paragraph (c) sits in "Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E"; a private company is outside it {MR-b}

-- src:8459 | (9) Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by
-- src:8460 | it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E —
-- src:8462 | (a) within 30 days after the passing of a resolution mentioned
-- src:8463 | in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E (as the case may be) the
-- src:8464 | directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a
-- src:8465 | copy of the resolution;
@ref s 76B(9)(a) (src:8459-8465)
GIVEN `the day the resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E was passed` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 76B(9)(a) the last day for the directors to lodge a copy of the resolution` MEANS
    `period: the last day of a period after` `the day the resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E was passed` 30 Days

-- src:8459 | (9) Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by
-- src:8460 | it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E —
-- src:8462 | (a) within 30 days after the passing of a resolution mentioned
-- src:8463 | in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E (as the case may be) the
-- src:8464 | directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a
-- src:8465 | copy of the resolution;
@ref s 76B(9)(a) (src:8459-8465)
GIVEN `the company is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E was passed` IS A DATE
      `the directors have lodged a copy of the resolution with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the copy of the resolution was lodged` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(9)(a) the directors have lodged a copy of the resolution in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (9) begins "Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by it"; a private company is outside it (its own rule is subsection (7)) {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the directors have lodged a copy of the resolution with the Registrar`
             AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the day the resolution mentioned in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E was passed` `the day the copy of the resolution was lodged` 30 Days
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the passing of a resolution ... the directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution" (a duty not met, the provision's own question) {F-B9} {MR-a}

