      `the date on which the shares are deemed to be purchased or acquired` IS A DATE
      `the directors have lodged a notice of purchase or acquisition with the Registrar` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day the notice of purchase or acquisition was lodged` IS A DATE
      notice IS A `s 76B(7)(b) notice of purchase or acquisition`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(9)(b) the directors have lodged a notice of purchase or acquisition in time` MEANS
    IF NOT `the company is a public company`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): subsection (9) begins "Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by it"; a private company is outside it {MR-b}
    ELSE (IF    `the directors have lodged a notice of purchase or acquisition with the Registrar`
             AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date on which the shares are deemed to be purchased or acquired` `the day the notice of purchase or acquisition was lodged` 30 Days
             AND `s 76B(7)(b) the notice of purchase or acquisition is in the prescribed form and has the particulars` notice EQUALS JUST TRUE
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "within 30 days after the purchase or acquisition of the shares, the directors of the company must lodge a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form with the following particulars" (a duty not met, the provision's own question; the particulars are the same nine as subsection (7)(b)) {F-B9} {MR-a}

§ `Section 76B(10): the Court's orders are not limited`

-- src:8505 | (10) Nothing in this section or in sections 76C to 76G is to be
-- src:8506 | construed so as to limit or affect an order of the Court made under any
-- src:8507 | section that requires a company to purchase or acquire its own shares.
@ref s 76B(10) (src:8505-8507)
GIVEN `the order of the Court requires the company to purchase or acquire its own shares` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(10) section 76B or sections 76C to 76G limit or affect the order of the Court` MEANS
    IF `the order of the Court requires the company to purchase or acquire its own shares`
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Nothing in this section or in sections 76C to 76G is to be construed so as to limit or affect an order of the Court made under any section that requires a company to purchase or acquire its own shares" (a flat negative) {F-B10} {MR-a}
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the subsection speaks only of an order that requires the company to purchase or acquire its own shares

§ `The seam to s 7(9)(ca): an interest of a company in its own shares`

-- s 7(9)(ca) (the keel) disregards "an interest of a company in its own shares if that interest is purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with
-- sections 76B to 76G (including treasury shares)". This function answers that fact: the acquisition is in accordance with the sections when the
-- power of subsection (1) holds, the section applies to the shares by subsection (2), the 20% limit is not exceeded, and a market, off-market or
-- contingent acquisition was authorised (the authority is the sections' own; the caller supplies its result).
-- When one of the four conditions fails it answers JUST FALSE (changed from NOTHING after the independent review, assumed, not ruled; fork line F-B11):
-- (ca) is introduced by "if", and the sections say what a failure is: s 76B(3) "must not exceed 20% ... unless", s 76E(1) "must not make a purchase or
-- acquisition ... unless ... authorised in advance", s 76F(2) "no purchase or acquisition ... is lawful".
-- It asks four conditions and not every condition of the sections: s 76B(7) (lodging with the Registrar) and s 76D(2A) (the consent of 75% of the holders of the class) are
-- procedural, and the text does not say what their breach does to the purchase, so a caller who has not met them can still get JUST TRUE here.
-- src:8314 | 76B.—(1) Despite section 76, a company may, in accordance with
-- src:8315 | this section and sections 76C to 76G, purchase or otherwise acquire
-- src:8316 | shares issued by it if it is expressly permitted to do so by its
-- src:8317 | constitution.
@ref s 76B(1) (src:8314-8317)
GIVEN `the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it under section 76B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number purchased or acquired exceeds the limit in section 76B(3) or (3B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised as section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 76B(1) the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` MEANS
    IF    `the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it under section 76B(1)`
      AND `section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares`
      AND (NOT `the number purchased or acquired exceeds the limit in section 76B(3) or (3B)`)
      AND `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised as section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): s 7(9)(ca) asks whether the interest was acquired "in accordance with sections 76B to 76G"; an acquisition that fails one of the four conditions is not in accordance with them ("must not ... unless", "is [not] lawful"); s 7 is the keel's {F-B11}

-- The keel's field is a plain BOOLEAN. A caller fills it from the answer above with `EQUALS JUST TRUE`, which carries JUST FALSE to FALSE and no NOTHING at all, because the function above never answers NOTHING.
-- No module calls this one: the keel cannot import a later part, and the seat asks the field as a question of its own.
@ref s 76B(1) (src:8314-8317)
GIVEN `the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it under section 76B(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number purchased or acquired exceeds the limit in section 76B(3) or (3B)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised as section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76B(1) the keel's s 7(9)(ca) field: the interest is in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` MEANS
    `s 76B(1) the interest is a company's interest in its own shares purchased or otherwise acquired in accordance with sections 76B to 76G` `the company may purchase or otherwise acquire shares issued by it under section 76B(1)` `section 76B and sections 76C to 76G apply to the shares` `the number purchased or acquired exceeds the limit in section 76B(3) or (3B)` `the purchase or acquisition has been authorised as section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E requires` EQUALS JUST TRUE

§ `Regulative rules: the directors' duties to lodge, s 76B(9)(a) and (b)`

DECLARE `s 76B act` IS ONE OF
    `s 76B(9)(a) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution`
    `s 76B(9)(b) lodge with the Registrar a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form with the particulars`

-- The clock of each rule is counted in days from the event the text names: day 0 is the day the resolution was passed (for (a)) or the day the
-- shares are deemed purchased or acquired (for (b)); "within 30 days after" ends on day 30 (P1 of the keel).
-- src:8459 | (9) Where a public company purchases or acquires shares issued by
-- src:8460 | it under section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E —
-- src:8462 | (a) within 30 days after the passing of a resolution mentioned
-- src:8463 | in section 76C, 76D, 76DA or 76E (as the case may be) the
-- src:8464 | directors of the company must lodge with the Registrar a
-- src:8465 | copy of the resolution;
@ref s 76B(9)(a) (src:8459-8465)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76B act`
`s 76B(9)(a) the directors must lodge a copy of the resolution within 30 days after it is passed` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 76B(9)(a) lodge with the Registrar a copy of the resolution`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not lodge a copy of the resolution with the Registrar within 30 days after it was passed"

-- src:8467 | (b) within 30 days after the purchase or acquisition of the
-- src:8468 | shares, the directors of the company must lodge a notice of
-- src:8469 | purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form with the
-- src:8470 | following particulars:
-- src:8472 | (i) the date of the purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8474 | (ii) the number of shares purchased or acquired;
-- src:8476 | (iii) the number of shares cancelled;
-- src:8478 | (iv) the number of shares held as treasury shares;
-- src:8480 | (v) the company’s issued share capital before the
-- src:8481 | purchase or acquisition;
-- src:8483 | (vi) the company’s issued share capital after the purchase
-- src:8484 | or acquisition;
-- src:8486 | (vii) the amount of consideration paid by the company for
-- src:8487 | the purchase or acquisition of the shares;
-- src:8489 | (viii) whether the shares were purchased or acquired out of
-- src:8490 | the profits or the capital of the company;
-- src:8492 | (ix) such other particulars as may be required in the
-- src:8493 | prescribed form; and
@ref s 76B(9)(b) (src:8467-8493)
GIVEN `the name of the director` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 76B act`
`s 76B(9)(b) the directors must lodge the notice of purchase or acquisition within 30 days after the purchase or acquisition` MEANS
    PARTY Director `the name of the director`
    MUST `s 76B(9)(b) lodge with the Registrar a notice of purchase or acquisition in the prescribed form with the particulars`
    WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Director `the name of the director` BECAUSE "the directors did not lodge a notice of purchase or acquisition with the Registrar within 30 days after the purchase or acquisition"
